Functional Interface:
it has exactly one abstract method, it represents a single operation or behaviour, implementation uses lambda functions, java introducted its functional programming support in java 8. the @FunctionalInterface annotation helps verify the interface rules. 

5 Types in Functional Interface: 1) predicate 2)function 3) consumer 4) supplier 5) Bifunction

consumer- accepts and does not return any value 

Anonymous function: without an explicit declared name, used to define behaviour without creating a seperate named method(to use it we use consumer here(functionalinterfacelo)), helps reduce unnecessary code in certain situations. 

We got a doubt whether the anonymous function is private? 
A) Anonymity means a function has no identifier (name) bound to it in the code definition. (e.g., function() {} or () => {}). 

Consumer interface: it accepts one input value, performs an operation on the received value, does not return any result, its abstract method is accept(), useful for displaying and processing information. 

Supplier interface: it does not accept any input, provides or returns a value when requested, its abstract method is get(), useful for generating or suplying values, it provides data whenever the application needs it. 

Predicate Interface: it accepts an input and checks a condition, always returnns a boolean value, its abstract method is test(), useful for validations and decision-making, it helps determine whether a particular condition is satisfied.
